
# Assignment 6: TLS-Enabled Chat System

## Available Chat Rooms:
- **KSU-Football** - Discuss KSU football games and news
- **Technology** - Technology discussions and programming  
- **General-Chat** - General conversation
- **Study-Group** - Academic study discussions
- **Gaming** - Video game discussions

## Setup Instructions:

1. Copy the files to your own directory.

2. Modify inet.h to reflect the host you are currently logged into.
   Also, modify the port numbers to be used to reduce the likelihood
   of conflicting with another server.

3. Compile the source code using the command: make

5. Start the directory server in the background: ./directoryServer5 &

6. Start chat servers for available topics in the background:
   ./chatServer5 KSU-Football &
   ./chatServer5 Technology &
   ./chatServer5 General-Chat &
   ./chatServer5 Study-Group &
   ./chatServer5 Gaming &

7. Start the client on the same or another host in the foreground: ./chatClient5

8. Remember to kill all servers before logging off.

## Certificate Verification:
- All connections use TLS encryption
- Client verifies server certificates match expected server type
- Directory server certificate contains "directory-server"
- Chat server certificates contain the specific room name
